<title>USA: Best Products financing approved.</title>
<headline>Best Products financing approved.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. Bankruptcy Court judge here on Thursday approved financing for Best Products Co Inc while the retail chain reorganizes its operations.</p>
<p>Richmond, Va.-based Best Products filed for protection from creditors under Chapter 11 on September 24, due to declining sales, mounting losses and lack of support from suppliers.</p>
<p>Judge Douglas Tice approved Best Products' $250 million financing secured from the CIT Group/Business Credit Inc. The judge had given preliminary approval on September 30.</p>
<p>Final approval was necessary for Best Products to purchase merchandise for the critical Christmas selling season.</p>
</text>
